Day 249/250: Minimum Cost to Convert String I

Problem Statement #2976

Problem Statement Explantion:

You are given two strings, source and target, both of length n, and three arrays: original, changed, and cost. These arrays describe the allowed character transformations:
You can change the character original[i] to changed[i] at a cost of cost[i].
Transformations can be chained (e.g., 'a' → 'b' → 'c').
The goal is to find the minimum total cost to convert the source string to the target string. If it is impossible to convert the string, return -1

Solution Approach:

This problem is effectively an All-Pairs Shortest Path problem on a directed weighted graph.

Graph Representation:

Treat the 26 lowercase English letters ('a' - 'z') as nodes in a graph.
The original, changed, and cost arrays represent the directed edges and their weights.
Since there might be multiple ways to transform character A to character B given in the input, we strictly store the minimum edge weight during initialization.

Floyd-Warshall Algorithm:

Since the number of nodes is very small (constant 26), we use the Floyd-Warshall algorithm to precompute the shortest path (minimum cost) between every pair of characters.
We initialize a 26x26 matrix dist where dist[i][j] is infinity, and dist[i][i] = 0.
After running the algorithm, dist[u][v] holds the minimum cost to convert character u to v via any sequence of intermediate changes.

Calculation:

Iterate through the source and target strings.
For every index i, check the cost to convert source[i] to target[i] using our precomputed dist matrix.
If any required transformation has a cost of infinity, return -1.
Otherwise, sum the costs. Note that the total can exceed a 32-bit integer, so we use long.

Here's the code:

class Solution {
    public long minimumCost(String source, String target, char[] original, char[] changed, int[] cost) {
        long[][] dist = new long[26][26];
        final long INF = Integer.MAX_VALUE;
        
        // Initialize distance matrix
        for (long[] row : dist) {
            Arrays.fill(row, INF);
        }
        for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
            dist[i][i] = 0;
        }
        
        // Build initial graph
        for (int i = 0; i < original.length; i++) {
            int u = original[i] - 'a';
            int v = changed[i] - 'a';
            dist[u][v] = Math.min(dist[u][v], cost[i]);
        }
        
        // Floyd-Warshall Algorithm
        for (int k = 0; k < 26; k++) {
            for (int i = 0; i < 26; i++) {
                for (int j = 0; j < 26; j++) {
                    if (dist[i][k] < INF && dist[k][j] < INF) {
                        dist[i][j] = Math.min(dist[i][j], dist[i][k] + dist[k][j]);
                    }
                }
            }
        }
        
        long totalCost = 0;
        int n = source.length();
        
        // Calculate total cost
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            int u = source.charAt(i) - 'a';
            int v = target.charAt(i) - 'a';
            
            if (u == v) continue;
            
            if (dist[u][v] >= INF) {
                return -1;
            }
            
            totalCost += dist[u][v];
        }
        
        return totalCost;
    }
}

Complexity:

Time Complexity: O(n+m)
Space Complexity: O(1)



